  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "FISHERINV computes (EXP(2y) - 1) / (EXP(2y) + 1), returning 0 for |y| < 2^-54 and saturating to +1 on overflow",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20527, FISHERINV(y) evaluates (EXP(2*y) - 1) / (EXP(2*y) + 1) using Excel's EXP rather than TANH(y) or 1 - 2/(EXP(2*y) + 1), saturating to +1 when EXP(2*y) overflows to infinity. Because EXP(2*y) rounds to 1 for |2*y| < 2^-53, tiny inputs such as 1e-100 return 0 instead of tanh(y) ~= y, and FISHERINV(1) returns 0x3fe85efab514f394 (1 ULP above TANH(1) = 0x3fe85efab514f393). All 2,087 full-bank FISHERINV rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence readings/excel-20527/bank2-answers-fisherinv-scalar.json (Excel 16.0 build 20527) and matched on 2,087/2,087 full-bank FISHERINV rows.",
